{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310789,"nonce":"KTWgF0CtmlObX8AOWZ9aoiK5gcc=","title":"G1 (loads/stores get a GEP) made LLVM auto-vectorise ordinary scalar Haxe loops, which retired the stated motive for hand-written SIMD ...","message":"**MEASURED at HEAD (2026-08-21).** After `4ba83731` (G1: give loads and stores a\nGEP so `inttoptr` stops blinding ScalarEvolution), LLVM auto-vectorises a plain\nscalar Haxe quantise loop **16 lanes wide**, emitting exactly the ops that were\nqueued to be added by hand:\n\n```llvm\n%90 = fptosi \u003c16 x double\u003e %89 to \u003c16 x i32\u003e\n%93 = trunc nsw  \u003c16 x i32\u003e  %92 to \u003c16 x i8\u003e\n%94 = xor        \u003c16 x i8\u003e   %93, splat (i8 -128)\nstore            \u003c16 x i8\u003e   %94, ptr %95\n```\n\n**So the \"87% of the quantise is a scalar store loop\" figure was measured\nBEFORE G1 and no longer describes HEAD.** Do not re-quote it. Any claim that a\nplain Haxe loop \"falls back to scalar\" must be re-checked against\n`RAYZOR_DUMP_LLVM_IR=1` (writes `/tmp/rayzor_llvm_ir_opt.ll`) before it is\nbelieved.\n\n**Where hand-written SIMD still earns its place:** wasm (no auto-vectoriser at\nall), Cranelift (none either), and loops LLVM cannot prove safe. Measured on\nthe quantise produce loop, 40000x4096 elements:\n\n| variant | ms |\n|---|---|\n| scalar, `Float` (f64) | 77 |\n| scalar, `Single` (f32) | 62 |\n| SIMD convert + saturating pack | 48 |\n\nAll three byte-identical (checksum 632750280). So explicit SIMD is still\n**1.6x** over auto-vectorised scalar — real, but not the 4.4x that was\npredicted from the pre-G1 measurement.\n\n**Second finding, systemic and unfixed:** `Mem.loadF32` is declared\n`:Float`, i.e. f64. Every plain-Haxe f32 kernel therefore widens each lane to\nf64 (`fpext \u003c16 x float\u003e to \u003c16 x double\u003e`) and does twice the vector work it\nneeds. Pinning the locals to `Single` gave 77 -\u003e 62 ms with a byte-identical\nchecksum. 75 `Mem.loadF32` call sites across 5 nue kernels (`Q4Matmul`,\n`Int8Matmul`, `FlashDecode`, `RoPE` (already Single), `Q8Cache`) — but nue's\nhot paths are already explicit SIMD, so the aggregate prize is the plain-Haxe\nperiphery only and is probably below this Mac's resolution. Runnable A/B:\n`compiler/tests/haxe/test_quantize_{bench,single,vector}.hx`.\n\nRelated: [[reference_kernel_replacement_acceptance_bar]],\n[[perf_haxe_kernel_pool_cooperation_blocker]],\n[[project_pure_haxe_tensor_ownership]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_g1_gep_made_plain_haxe_loops_vectorise` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}